@tradition tiles-ladder
// Tiles ladder (0.60.7, the user's pick): a friendly weekly Tiles round-robin on Saturday afternoons in the bow lounge,
// with a chalkboard for the week's winner. Olu Farouk keeps the ladder. The boards are Tiles night's (decor tilesNight);
// the results would be the Tiles engineer's (section 23).
k: 450
title: Tiles ladder
when: weekly saturday
at: 15:00-16:30
min: 25
jitter: 15
where: 3 room Bow lounge: lounge-seat
hold: 1
who: farouk-olu always, rina 90%, lounge-regular 40%, everyone 10%
anim: play
host: farouk-olu
from: farouk-olu
ties: decor tilesNight
invite: host=farouk-olu odds=30% line="Tiles ladder this afternoon. You're on the board. Bottom rung, but on the board."

== mail
- Tiles ladder tomorrow, {time}, in the bow lounge. Round-robin, friendly. The winner's name goes on the chalkboard for a week.

== ask
- Tiles ladder this afternoon. I'm on rung four. Rung four!   #funny
- Coming to the ladder? Olu's got a board waiting.
- Saturday Tiles. Friendly, Olu says. Olu keeps score in pen.   #funny

== here
- Your move. The ladder waits for no one.   #funny
- Good game. Next table, please.
- One more win and I'm on the chalkboard.

== thanks
- You play a round of the Tiles ladder. Olu writes your result on the chalkboard, neatly.

== chatter
- Rina's been top of the ladder three weeks. Someone stop her.   #funny
- The ladder's chalkboard is the most read thing on the ship.   #funny
